DEADQUOTE_SO_RUN_OVER_BY_VEHICLE	Field Guide\nYou were run over by a vehicle.\nWatch for moving enemy vehicles.
DEADQUOTE_SO_STEALTH_LOOK_FOR_ENEMIES	Field Guide\nFind enemies near or facing your target before firing. Take out the group quickly to stay hidden.
DEADQUOTE_SO_STEALTH_STAY_LOW	Field Guide\nStay low. Standing or running makes you easier to see and hear.
DEADQUOTE_SO_STEALTH_USE_SILENCERS	Field Guide\nUse suppressors. Grenades and unsuppressed weapons draw attention.
DEADQUOTE_SO_CLAYMORE_ENEMIES_SHOOT	Field Guide\nEnemies will shoot exposed claymores. Place yours behind cover.
DEADQUOTE_SO_CLAYMORE_POINT_ENEMY	Field Guide\nAim a claymore's red beams toward the enemy's approach.
DEADQUOTE_SO_TURRET_PLACEMENT	Field Guide\nProtect your turrets. Place them behind cover to avoid flanking attacks.
DEADQUOTE_PLAYER_DISCONNECTED	Your partner has left the game.
DEADQUOTE_IF_AN_INJURY_HAS_TO_BE	If an injury has to be done to a man it should be so severe that his vengeance need not be feared. - Machiavelli
DEADQUOTE_LIVE_WELL_IT_IS_THE_GREATEST	Live well. It is the greatest revenge. - The Talmud
DEADQUOTE_REVENGE_AT_FIRST_THOUGH	Revenge, at first though sweet, Bitter ere long back on itself recoils. - John Milton
DEADQUOTE_BEFORE_YOU_EMBARK_UPON	Before you embark upon a journey of revenge, you should first dig two graves. - Confucius
DEADQUOTE_DISSENT_REBELLION_AND	...dissent, rebellion, and all-around hell-raising remain the true duty of patriots. - Barbara Ehrenreich
DEADQUOTE_A_CITIZEN_OF_AMERICA	A citizen of America will cross the ocean to fight for democracy, but won't cross the street to vote... - Bill Vaughan
DEADQUOTE_I_WAS_BORN_AN_AMERICAN	I was born an American; I will live an American; I shall die an American! - Daniel Webster
DEADQUOTE_WE_MUST_NOT_CONFUSE_DISSENT	We must not confuse dissent with disloyalty. - Edward R. Murrow
DEADQUOTE_PATRIOTISM_IS_YOUR_CONVICTION	Patriotism is your conviction that this country is superior to all others because you were born in it. - George Bernard Shaw
DEADQUOTE_PATRIOTISM_IS_A_ARBITRARY	Patriotism is a arbitrary veneration of real estate above principles. - George Jean Nathan
DEADQUOTE_A_MANS_FEET_MUST_BE_PLANTED	A man's feet must be planted in his country, but his eyes should survey the world. - George Santayana
DEADQUOTE_PATRIOTISM_RUINS_HISTORY	Patriotism ruins history. - Goethe
DEADQUOTE_ASK_NOT_WHAT_YOUR_COUNTRY	Ask not what your country can do for you, but what you can do for your country. - John F. Kennedy
DEADQUOTE_THE_NATION_IS_DIVIDED	The nation is divided, half patriots and half traitors, and no man can tell which from which. - Mark Twain
DEADQUOTE_IF_YOU_WANT_A_SYMBOLIC	If you want a symbolic gesture, don't burn the flag; wash it. - Norman Thomas
DEADQUOTE_I_WILL_FIGHT_FOR_MY_COUNTRY	I will fight for my country, but I will not lie for her. - Zora Neale Hurston
DEADQUOTE_PATRIOTISM_IS_SUPPORTING	Patriotism is supporting your country all the time, and your government when it deserves it. - Mark Twain
DEADQUOTE_A_NATION_REVEALS_ITSELF	A nation reveals itself not only by the men it produces but also by the men it honors, the men it remembers. - John F. Kennedy
DEADQUOTE_I_ONLY_REGRET_THAT_I	I only regret that I have but one life to give for my country. - Nathan Hale
DEADQUOTE_PATRIOTISM_VARIES_FROM	Patriotism varies, from a noble devotion to a moral lunacy. - W.R. Inge
DEADQUOTE_IF_YOU_ARE_ASHAMED_TO	If you are ashamed to stand by your colors, you had better seek another flag. - Anonymous
DEADQUOTE_NATIONALISM_IS_AN_INFANTILE	Nationalism is an infantile disease.  It is the measles of mankind. - Albert Einstein
DEADQUOTE_IF_OUR_COUNTRY_IS_WORTH	If our country is worth dying for in time of war let us resolve that it is truly worth living for in time of peace. - Hamilton Fish
DEADQUOTE_IT_IS_LAMENTABLE_THAT	It is lamentable, that to be a good patriot one must become the enemy of the rest of mankind. - Voltaire
DEADQUOTE_TRADITIONAL_NATIONALISM	Traditional nationalism cannot survive the fissioning of the atom. One world or none. - Stuart Chase
DEADQUOTE_WE_KNOW_WHERE_THEY_ARE	We know where they are. They're in the area around Tikrit and Baghdad and east, west, south and north somewhat. - Donald Rumsfeld
DEADQUOTE_I_WOULD_NOT_SAY_THAT	I would not say that the future is necessarily less predictable than the past. I think the past was not predictable when it started. - Donald Rumsfeld
DEADQUOTE_IT_IS_EASY_TO_TAKE_LIBERTY	It is easy to take liberty for granted, when you have never had it taken from you. - Dick Cheney
DEADQUOTE_PRINCIPLE_IS_OK_UP_TO	Principle is OK up to a certain point, but principle doesn't do any good if you lose. - Dick Cheney
DEADQUOTE_I_LOVE_AMERICA_MORE_THAN	I love America more than any other country in this world; and, exactly for this reason, I insist on the right to criticize her perpetually. - James Baldwin
DEADQUOTE_AS_WE_EXPRESS_OUR_GRATITUDE	As we express our gratitude, we must never forget that the highest appreciation is not to utter words, but to live by them. - John F. Kennedy
